WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.550
<i>This is the town of Tajimi, 
in Gifu prefecture.</i>

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.840
<i>It's been home to some of the 
hottest days Japan's ever seen...</i>

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.890
<i>But in October, it's pretty comfortable.</i>

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:10.720
<i>It's a town all about ceramics.</i>

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:15.020
<i>My name is Toyokawa Himeno. 
I moved here in April,</i>

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:17.040
<i>and after joining my school's pottery club,</i>

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.610
<i>I had my first experiencing 
with making ceramics!</i>

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:25.210
<i>After learning that my dearly 
departed Mom was an amazing potter,</i>

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.860
<i>I started trying a lot of different things,</i>

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.960
<i>almost like she was encouraging me to...</i>

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.350
<i>And while it wasn't a smooth trip,</i>

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.620
<i>I was finally able to make 
something I was proud of.</i>

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.450
<i>Even if it broke.</i>

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:45.600
<i>Now it feels like I'm finally at the 
starting line for my pottery journey.</i>

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.450
Cutting it kinda close...

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.770
Watch out for traffic.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:52.950
Okay!

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.440
What's that on your strap?

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.950
Pretty, isn't it?

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.210
It's a piece of the cushion that you broke!

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.300
Oh, that's what you did with it?

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:08.470
I really love how the 
crystalline glaze turned out!

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.450
What're you going to make next?

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.660
Well, next...

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.860
I can't think of anything!

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:22.500
I won't be able to come up with 
any ideas without some inspiration.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.600
Like when your mug got broke, 
or when the contest came up.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.990
Anyway, I'm heading out!

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:30.960
Good morning!

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:06.870
<b>Let's Go! Down the Path of Pottery</b>

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.120
I want to make something 
more wonderful next time...

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.860
What do you mean, exactly?

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:14.890
Well, y'know...

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.280
I can't think of anything!

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.240
I'm sure it'll be okay.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:25.260
You mentioned how much you enjoyed 
a lot of people seeing your piece, right?

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.900
As long as you still feel the same way...

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:29.280
Come in!

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.150
We meet again, Aoki-san!

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.640
Matsuse-san?

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.890
Is this a friend of Touko-senpai's?

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:39.780
I don't know if I'd say that...

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.080
Our relationship is far more than that.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.920
I might live in Aichi now,

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:46.850
but there was a time where we 
were best friends here in Gifu,

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:49.490
who competed against each other in pottery!

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:51.580
No, it was more than that.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.670
We were friends for life! Honored friends!

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:59.230
So, uh, what brings you by? And so suddenly.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:01.300
I wanted to tell you something.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:04.850
I saw your winning piece 
from that recent contest.

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:07.150
It was magnificent!

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:08.800
Th-Thank you...

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:13.320
But it's not good enough 
to win the grand prize!

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:17.030
I could see indecision in the 
way the glaze was applied!

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:18.550
You know why, don't you?

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.020
And?

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:31.200
I want you to submit something 
for the exhibition

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.630
that's going to be run by your 
grandfather in November!

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:36.070
I'll be submitting, too, and 
if you don't, then we're through!

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.340
Well, I guess that means we're through.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:40.880
No! Never!

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.330
I'll be waiting!

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.360
It feels like a storm passed through...

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:55.910
I didn't know you had a friend like that!

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:57.310
Is she always that way?

00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:59.780
She's not a bad person.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:02.430
She gave me some important advice, once.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.330
She's a little too intense for me, though.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:08.740
Come on. Let's get back to the wheel.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.470
Touko-senpai.

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:27.670
Yes?

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:31.830
What was the advice that 
Matsuse-san gave you?

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.390
"Don't concentrate on the finger."

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:36.590
"Or you'll miss the moon."

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.080
I don't follow, at all.

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:44.410
This is the way I interpreted it...

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:48.370
"Don't just focus on improving 
your technical skills."

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:50.850
"That's not the real core of pottery."

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:55.780
Then what is the real core?

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:58.990
I guess Aoki-senpai didn't 
make that clear, huh?

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:03.620
"A good question. It's probably something 
that needs to be figured out by yourself."

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:06.330
That was great! You sounded 
just like Touko-senpai!

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:07.430
Huh?

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.470
You should try that in 
the club room next time!

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.050
Everyone would think it's great!

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.300
I am not doing that!

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.300
Aw, why not?

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.420
Can't, I just can't, no way!

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.060
See ya!

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.530
I'm home.

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.250
Welcome back.

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:23.670
Sensei! Thanks for coming by.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:26.920
I really do see the resemblance.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.450
Your cushion had amazing colors.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:33.120
You're Kusano-sensei, right?

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.700
You were the pottery club adviser last year!

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:39.130
I appreciate your evaluation 
during the contest.

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:44.980
During the judging, I saw your 
name and realized who you were.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:47.540
Toyokawa and Tokikawa's daughter.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.730
You know each other?

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:52.720
He was two years ahead
 of us in high school.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.960
I was in the pottery club with your mother.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:59.370
And I'm ten years Kusano-sensei's junior.

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:02.080
Wait, you went to the same school, too?!

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.870
Sure did. And I used to hang 
out with the pottery club.

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:08.050
The same way Naruse-san does, now.

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:11.980
That was around the time your 
mom came back to town...

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:20.710
For you!

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:27.570
She had a new project underway, and the 
pottery club ended up helping her.

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:30.260
It seemed like fun, so I pitched in, too.

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:33.590
Did you meet Dad back then, too?

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:36.360
Yep! I met them both at the time!

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:39.120
Although I didn't talk too much with them.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:43.480
Didn't you write a poem about what happened?

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.020
You were in the literature club, right?

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:47.970
Please don't bring up that kind of thing 
in front of one of my students!

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:50.310
It's too embarrassing!

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:53.480
Um, can I ask you something?

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:02.770
The core of pottery, huh?

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:07.640
Considering how subjective it is, 
there's no easy explanation...

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:09.390
That makes sense.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:16.020
But maybe some stories about your mom 
will help you figure something out?

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.250
I'd love to hear about her!

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:20.970
Nothing too weird, okay?

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:22.760
Of course not!

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:26.090
Do you remember when she suddenly started 
drinking coffee in her third year?

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:28.770
Oh, I remember that!

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:34.070
I was attending art school in Tokyo, 
but had come back for summer vacation.

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:36.640
And when I checked out the club room...

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.800
Wh-What the heck?!

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:54.840
Tokikawa! Tokikawa, wake up!

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:59.330
Did you seriously just crash here?

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:03.800
Hey, Kusano-senpai! It's been a while.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:05.880
What exactly happened here?

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:09.310
Oh, well, I started making 
them on Saturday...

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.560
And fell asleep at some point!

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:14.550
You realize it's Monday afternoon, right?

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:16.610
Did you attend any of your classes?

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:22.560
I skipped everything!

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:26.530
Mom could be pretty bold, huh?

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:29.770
She was apparently trying every 
different shape that came to mind,

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:32.710
in order to find the cup that'd 
make coffee taste the best.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:35.830
And after firing them all, 
she tried them all out...

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:39.420
I think this one might be it...

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:47.400
But it doesn't really feel like 
a definitive winner, y'know?

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:50.940
And then she stopped coming 
by the club room...

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:56.320
Because she was checking out 
all of the cafes in town.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:01.650
Which made a great excuse for a bunch 
of dates, if I remember right.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:02.800
Is that what happened?

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.630
Here we go again...

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:09.310
Although it was fun riding around 
on the back of her scooter.

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:13.500
Wait, when you rode together 
you would cling to her?

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:14.910
To her shoulders! That's all!

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:16.860
Coffee
Spaghetti

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:18.050
Anyway, she would drink a cup coffee,

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.990
and then afterwards she would 
tell me her in-depth opinion...

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:20.990
Café Mokuba

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:23.850
It wasn't at all romantic.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.630
She'd just take a bunch of notes, 
and we'd be off to the next spot.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:29.190
And did it actually help her?

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:32.120
See, that's the really incredible thing.

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:37.680
Tokikawa!

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:40.510
Oh, senpai! Welcome.

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:43.130
Are you trying to turn the 
club room into a tea house?

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:45.620
Why'd you make so many of the same cup?

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:47.760
They're not the same.

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:54.370
I've made slight changes to the 
inside of the cup every time.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:55.780
Seriously?

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:59.460
I thought that it'd be 
fun to do latte art, too,

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:01.220
and then I realized how important convection is.

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:05.900
I'm trying to make the ultimate cup, 
with the ideal convection heating!

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:09.530
<i>You're really amazing.</i>

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:15.210
And after she managed to come up 
with her ultimate cup,

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:18.060
she took it around to 
cafés all over town...

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:19.700
It was a huge hit.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:21.530
That's incredible.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:24.310
Whatever happened to that cup?

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:25.780
It's gone missing.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:27.340
Seriously?

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:29.840
She said she was going to give it to me,

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:33.640
but then something else grabbed her 
attention, and it got lost in the process.

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:34.910
That sounds like her.

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:41.060
Maybe I should get out and 
do some legwork, too...

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:46.820
I mean, Mom would run around all over Tajimi

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:49.520
when she didn't know what 
she wanted to make, right?

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:55.740
Maybe I should try doing that
 until I find the right inspiration!

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.120
Sounds good to me.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:08.260
You might find the core of 
your pottery if you do that.

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:12.210
All of these were made by her, too, right?

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:13.110
Yes.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.950
Can I have this one, Toyokawa?

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:17.480
Go right on ahead.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:20.720
It's been twenty years...

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:32.430
I think things are going to get really fun!

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:37.140
I'm going to try walking all over town!

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:43.150
In that case, once you make something 
good, we can put it right there.

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:51.180
It'll be the spot for 
Toyokawa Himeno's masterpiece.

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:54.650
That kind of makes me nervous...

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:56.930
But, yeah! Sounds good!

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:06.360
<i>I wonder what I'm going to make.</i>

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.620
<i>I'm looking forward to it!</i>

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:27.320
The bob-cut haired girl, and the sole member

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:35.270
<b>Mini Mini Pottery Club</b>

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:30.600
of the bob-cut haired girl 
study club, the plain girl...

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:33.950
But they happen to share a certain secret!

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:36.230
Next time is "My Paradise."

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:37.350
<b>Next Time:</b>

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:39.930
<b>My Paradise</b>

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:39.360
Let this miraculous story 
be engraved on your heart!
